AKA "see you in Hell".

EFFECT: levelports target to random level where Valley of Dead < level
<= bottom of maze.
              No effect within Gehennom or on Planes.
Benefits:   Consigns your nemesis to the "tenth level of hell".

You zap the black wand!   -more-
a fiery circle opens beneath the archlich! -more-
the archlich screams as a hundred demons drag him to the bowels of
hell! -more-
the portal closes.

Problem:  Of course,  you're still going to have to fight that nemesis
later, in Gehennom.  You've only postponed the battle, not ended it.

So you could, for example, send Master Kaen to Gehennom.  The bad news
is that Master Kaen may not be any easier alongside Orcus -- and if the
gate works, Orcus and Demogorgon.

Other side benefit:  good way to get to the bottom of the maze quickly.

Other side benefit:  So Gehennom's boring, is it?   Not after you've
banished a dozen or so arch-liches, Master Kaen, and an archon or two
it isn't!

Nasty effects:
-- Can be used by demons, imps etc. outside of hell as an escape wand.
Could be unpleasant if it's carrying something important to you.   Used
as attack wand by other monsters?  Or simply carried, a la wand of
opening?

-- If used as an attack wand,  Not a good thing to have zapped at you
-- unless you have magic resistance. In which case, it's less
game-ending than, say, a ray of death or a disintegration beam, as the
subject still has a chance (however small) to get back out and salvage
the game.

-- Not a good thing to zap yourself with.
-- If you zap your pet with it, expect it NOT to be tame or peaceful
the next time you meet it.  For some reason, pets don't appreciate
unexpected trips to the lower planes.

